= Automated market maker — Simple =

An automated market maker is a market mechanism that uses rules or formulas to trade against available liquidity instead of matching every buyer directly with a seller. Many DeFi AMMs use pools supplied by liquidity providers.

'''Important boundary:''' AMM ≠ constant-product market maker only.

== Sources ==
* Bank for International Settlements, “Trading in the DeFi era: automated market-maker” (2021).
